      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with Jeremy on the follow-on CL.  The devicetree should only be specifying the GPIO pin, using a `gpios` property.  For the non-power buttons, the interrupt handler is always the same, so it doesn\u0027t need to be in the devicetree.\n\nAlso, the flags field isn\u0027t required, because Zephyr already specifies active-high/active-low with the GPIOs.\n\nThe button name appears to be a fixed value so, that can also be removed.",
